---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import AmazonButton from '../../components/AmazonButton.astro';
import PlannerCTA from '../../components/PlannerCTA.astro';

const faqSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do I check an infrared sauna blanket for a recall?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Find the exact brand, model number, controller description, and serial number on the product. Compare all of them with the current CPSC recall notice before buying or using the blanket. A brand name alone is not enough because recalls can apply to specific models or controllers."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How long should I use an infrared sauna blanket?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Use the time, temperature, clothing, surface, and supervision instructions in the exact model's current manual. There is no responsible universal session length for every blanket and user."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is an infrared sauna blanket the same as a sauna room?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "No. A blanket is a close-contact heated product used while lying down. A sauna room heats a larger occupied space and has different electrical, ventilation, seating, and operating requirements. Compare the experience and instructions as separate product categories."
      }
    }
  ]
};
---
<Base
  title="Best Infrared Sauna Blanket: Check Safety and Recalls First"
  description="Compare current infrared sauna blankets by recall status, model-specific instructions, electrical requirements, controls, cleaning, warranty, and returns."
  canonical="/guides/best-infrared-sauna-blanket"
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />

  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3">Best Infrared Sauna Blanket: Check Safety and Recalls First</h1>
    <p class="text-stone-500 mb-8">Reviewed August 2026 &mdash; Backyard Sauna Pro</p>

    <div class="bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-xl p-5 mb-8 text-sm text-stone-700">
      <strong>Affiliate disclosure:</strong> Some product links are affiliate links. If you buy through one, we may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. We have not physically tested these blankets. This guide compares current published specifications, instructions, and federal recall information.
    </div>

    <p class="text-lg text-stone-700 mb-4">A sauna blanket is easy to store, but it is still a heated electrical product used in close contact with the body. Start with the exact model and controller. Then check recalls, the current manual, placement requirements, and the return policy.</p>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-8">That order matters more than a “best overall” badge. Two recent federal recalls covered specific sauna blankets because of overheating, fire, and burn hazards.</p>

    <aside class="border border-red-200 bg-red-50 rounded-xl p-5 mb-10" aria-label="Current sauna blanket recall warning">
      <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-red-800 mb-2">Recall check required</p>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3">Match the model, controller, and serial number</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-sm text-stone-700">
        <li>The CPSC recalled specified <strong>LifePro BioRemedy</strong> blankets with listed model numbers and a gray-faced controller in October 2025. The notice says to stop using and unplug affected units.</li>
        <li>The CPSC recalled the <strong>SLF model 30065TAR</strong> with serial number <strong>WF2236430065</strong> in May 2026. The notice says to stop using it and contact Tzumi for a replacement.</li>
        <li>A used listing that hides the model or controller is not ready to buy. Ask for clear photos of every identification label first.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3 mt-4 text-sm font-semibold">
        <a href="https://www.cpsc.gov/Recalls/2026/Lifepro-Fitness-Recalls-Bioremedy-Infrared-Sauna-Blankets-Due-to-Risk-of-Burn-Injuries" class="text-red-800 hover:underline" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the LifePro BioRemedy recall</a>
        <a href="https://www.cpsc.gov/Recalls/2026/Tzumi-Electronics-Recalls-SLF-Sauna-Blankets-Due-to-Fire-and-Burn-Hazards" class="text-red-800 hover:underline" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the SLF recall</a>
      </div>
    </aside>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-4">How these options were selected</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-4">An option belongs here only when a current manufacturer page identifies the product and publishes enough detail to investigate it. We compare:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-stone-700 mb-6">
      <li>exact product identity and whether it matches a current recall;</li>
      <li>voltage, wattage, controller, heat levels, timer, and auto-shutoff information;</li>
      <li>required surface, clothing or liner, setup, cooling, cleaning, and storage instructions;</li>
      <li>published dimensions and fit;</li>
      <li>warranty, returns, support, and a current purchase route.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-sm text-stone-600 mb-8">Manufacturer wellness claims are not treated as independently proven facts. Read our <a href="/how-we-review/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">review methodology</a>.</p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-5">Current blankets to investigate</h2>
    <div class="space-y-5 mb-10">
      <section class="border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-5 bg-white">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-amber-700 uppercase tracking-wide mb-1">Detailed published specifications</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">HigherDOSE Infrared Sauna Blanket</h3>
        <p class="text-stone-600 mb-3">The current U.S. manufacturer page lists one heat zone, nine levels, heating up to 175&deg;F, a one-hour timer, 100-120V operation, 350-420 watts, and a one-year limited warranty. It also directs users to place the blanket on a heat-safe surface and keep the body covered with clothing or the brand's insert.</p>
        <p class="text-stone-600 mb-4"><strong>Verify before buying:</strong> the current manual, body-fit limits, surface requirements, controller and auto-shutoff behavior, cleaning method, warranty exclusions, and return conditions. Treat the brand's detox, recovery, and other wellness statements as marketing claims unless supported separately.</p>
        <AmazonButton asin="B09M8YQ4KB" variant="primary" label="Check the current HigherDOSE listing" ctaPosition="infrared_blanket_higherdose" />
        <p class="text-xs text-stone-500 mt-3"><a href="https://higherdose.com/products/infrared-sauna-blanket" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline" rel="noopener noreferrer">Review the manufacturer's specifications and instructions</a></p>
      </section>

      <section class="border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-5 bg-white">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-stone-600 uppercase tracking-wide mb-1">Current model with a recall distinction</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">LifePro RejuvaWrap</h3>
        <p class="text-stone-600 mb-3">LifePro's current page identifies the RejuvaWrap separately from the recalled BioRemedy. It lists adult use, nine heat levels, a 5-60 minute timer, a wired controller that remains plugged in, and placement on a heat-resistant surface.</p>
        <p class="text-stone-600 mb-4"><strong>Verify before buying:</strong> that the item is the RejuvaWrap shown on the current listing, not a recalled BioRemedy; the exact model label; the latest manual; fit; power requirements; cleaning; warranty; and return terms. Do not accept a seller's “new version” description without label photos.</p>
        <AmazonButton asin="B0BX7HLCYQ" variant="primary" label="Check the current RejuvaWrap listing" ctaPosition="infrared_blanket_rejuvawrap" />
        <p class="text-xs text-stone-500 mt-3"><a href="https://lifeprofitness.com/products/rejuvawrap" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline" rel="noopener noreferrer">Review the manufacturer's current RejuvaWrap page</a></p>
      </section>

      <section class="border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-5 bg-white">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-stone-600 uppercase tracking-wide mb-1">Different category: portable steam tent</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">SereneLife Portable Steam Sauna</h3>
        <p class="text-stone-600 mb-3">This is not an infrared blanket. It uses a separate steam generator and an enclosed tent, so its burn, hose, steam-diffuser, setup, cleaning, and storage questions are different. Compare it only if you prefer seated steam heat over lying inside a heated wrap.</p>
        <p class="text-stone-600 mb-4"><strong>Verify before buying:</strong> exact model and current manual, steam-hose routing, diffuser placement, chair limits, electrical requirements, cleaning, and recall status.</p>
        <AmazonButton asin="B084GY5CHB" variant="primary" label="Check the current SereneLife listing" ctaPosition="infrared_blanket_steam_alternative" />
      </section>
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-4">Six checks before you buy</h2>

    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-stone-900 mt-6 mb-2">1. Record the identification labels</h3>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-4">Save photos of the product label, controller, model number, serial number, and receipt. Compare them with current CPSC notices before purchase and again if the manufacturer announces a remedy later.</p>

    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-stone-900 mt-6 mb-2">2. Read the exact manual before ordering</h3>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-4">The manual should answer where the blanket can lie, what must cover the body, whether preheating is allowed, how the controller is positioned, who should not use the product, and how it cools and stores. A generic marketplace description is not a substitute.</p>

    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-stone-900 mt-6 mb-2">3. Check the electrical setup</h3>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-4">Match the voltage and plug to the intended outlet. Follow the model's rules for extension cords, power strips, controller placement, moisture, folding, and supervision. Stop using a unit with damaged wiring, hot spots, unusual odor, controller faults, or material damage, and contact the manufacturer.</p>

    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-stone-900 mt-6 mb-2">4. Test fit without guessing</h3>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-4">Compare your height and body position with the published dimensions. Check neck opening, zipper access, arm access, and whether you can exit without struggling. Do not treat “one size fits all” as a measurement.</p>

    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-stone-900 mt-6 mb-2">5. Ask what “low EMF” means</h3>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-4">A useful report identifies the test method, instrument, units, measurement distance, heat setting, locations tested, laboratory, and date. A badge without those details is difficult to compare. EMF language should not replace the recall, wiring, surface, temperature-control, and exit checks above.</p>

    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-stone-900 mt-6 mb-2">6. Price the exit path</h3>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-8">Confirm the return window, return-shipping responsibility, restocking terms, warranty duration, covered parts, replacement process, and support contact. Keep the box until you have inspected the unit and confirmed it matches the order.</p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-4">Use the model's instructions, not a universal routine</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-4">Session time, heat level, clothing, preheating, surface, hydration, supervision, cooling, and cleaning vary by model. Follow the current manual. If a health condition, medication, pregnancy, heat sensitivity, or mobility issue could affect heat exposure or exiting the blanket, discuss the product with an appropriate clinician before use.</p>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-8">Stop immediately if the blanket overheats, smells unusual, discolors, damages the surface beneath it, produces a controller error, or becomes difficult to exit. Unplug it when the instructions say to do so and contact the manufacturer.</p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-4">Blanket or sauna room?</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-4">Choose a blanket when compact storage and a lower-complexity setup matter most. Choose a room when you want seated space, a different heat experience, shared use, and a permanent installation. A room requires more planning, but it also gives you model-specific bench, heater, ventilation, electrical, and site choices that a blanket does not.</p>

    <PlannerCTA
      source="infrared_blanket_after_scope"
      heading="Considering a sauna room instead?"
      description="Build a free project brief with your site, available space, heat preference, utilities, budget, timeline, delivery access, and installation needs."
    />

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-4">Primary and current product sources</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-sm text-stone-700 mb-8">
      <li><a href="https://www.cpsc.gov/Recalls/2026/Lifepro-Fitness-Recalls-Bioremedy-Infrared-Sauna-Blankets-Due-to-Risk-of-Burn-Injuries" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline" rel="noopener noreferrer">CPSC: LifePro BioRemedy recall, October 23, 2025</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.cpsc.gov/Recalls/2026/Tzumi-Electronics-Recalls-SLF-Sauna-Blankets-Due-to-Fire-and-Burn-Hazards" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline" rel="noopener noreferrer">CPSC: SLF sauna blanket recall, May 28, 2026</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://higherdose.com/products/infrared-sauna-blanket" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline" rel="noopener noreferrer">HigherDOSE: current product specifications and instructions</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://lifeprofitness.com/products/rejuvawrap" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline" rel="noopener noreferrer">LifePro: current RejuvaWrap specifications and instructions</a></li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-4">FAQ</h2>
    <div class="space-y-5">
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-1">How do I check a blanket for a recall?</h3>
        <p class="text-stone-700">Match the brand, model number, controller description, and serial number against the current CPSC notice. If a seller will not show the labels, skip the listing.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-1">How long should I use an infrared sauna blanket?</h3>
        <p class="text-stone-700">Use the time and heat limits in the exact model's current manual. Do not copy a routine from another blanket or a sauna room.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-1">Is a blanket the same as a sauna room?</h3>
        <p class="text-stone-700">No. A blanket is a close-contact heated product. A room heats an occupied space and has different controls, installation requirements, and ways to sit or move.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-stone-50 border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-6 mt-10">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">Continue comparing</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
        <li><a href="/guides/best-portable-sauna/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Portable Sauna Buying Guide</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/best-indoor-sauna-kits/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Indoor Sauna Kit Buying Guide</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/infrared-vs-traditional-sauna/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Traditional vs. Infrared Sauna</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/sauna-cost/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Complete Sauna Project Budget</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
